  categories:
  - categoryName: Articles
    contentList:
    - "starvationArticle\r\nQuacklands Goes Hungry\r\nA rise in starvation across
      Quacklands has left the population in utter disarray. One civilian tried to
      help out their fellow ducks by donating some of their food which resulted in
      them starving as well. Another states \u201CI don\u2019t know what I\u2019m
      going to do?! Do you think biting into the water will work?\u201D Our editors
      have no idea. \r\nStarvation\r\n&\r\nmentalHealthArticle\r\nQuacklands In Despair\r\nOverworked
      and under-crumbed. The new mayor appears to think that working us like chickens
      will benefit the community. Now, it seems Quacklands is facing a major lapse
      in morale, which, if ignored, could prove fatal for even the most resilient
      citizens. I myself have a message for the mayor from the people of Quacklands:
      If you\u2019re not careful, we won\u2019t be the only ones that perish.\r\nMentalHealthCrisis\r\n&\r\nnewMayorArticle\r\nNew
      Mayor Installed\r\nAfter our previous mayor suddenly disappeared, someone new
      has flown in to pick up where he left off! We welcome our new mayor and wish
      them the best of luck! With a fresh pair of eyes hopefully some real improvement
      can be brought to our great land. They\u2019d better get to work fast, unless
      they want to end up like the last mayor.\r\nRequired\r\n&\r\nfarmArticle\r\nThe
      Wheat is finally over\r\nOur dear mayor has introduced a new technique to us
      called farming. It's where you put stuff into the ground and food grows from
      it. Our team is not sure of how it works but we ate it with no questions asked!
      The crumbies from the ground taste pretty good but it\u2019s a lot of work.
      \u201CWhy would anyone do this?\u201D one civilian asked, \u201CAll this time
      working leaves me less time to bob my head and shake my tail!\u201D This reporter
      wonders what the mayor's next move is after all this work.\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nnestArticle\r\nExtraordi-nest-y
      \r\nIt seems like our mayor can\u2019t get enough of us, folks! They started
      building a nest for us to start repopulating ooh la la. Now you can spend time
      with your partner and make a baby out in the open. One civilian commented,
      \u201Chey, should this even be allowed?\u201D\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nplaygroundArticle\r\nGetting
      into the Swing of Things\r\nThank honk that we can finally do something other
      than working, all of these new developments were making this journalist's beak
      hurt. So long are the days of just wandering around in the sun, we now have
      a thing called playgrounds to keep us occupied. I\u2019m not familiar with
      these foreign games that the mayor has introduced to us but I give these playgrounds
      4.5 quacks out of 5.\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\ngoldenCornArticle\r\nThis May Sound
      a Little Corny\r\nI guess we haven\u2019t been working well enough to please
      our mayor's expectations. As you may have noticed there is now a gold corn
      in our land. I thought it was for eating but it turns out that it is a mild
      symbol of oppression telling us to work harder. Hopefully our mayor just wants
      to see us reach our full potential but I will admit the statue is beautiful.
      I wish I could eat it though, why make something edible if it\u2019s not meant
      to be eaten?!\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\ncompostArticle\r\nDon\u2019t Let Your Scraps
      go to Waste\r\nWho knew garbage could be so useful! The mayor installed compost
      sites throughout the land to increase the production of our farms. Now we\u2019ll
      be gaining MORE crumbies to boost our economy, whatever an economy is. Apparently
      number go up means something good! I can\u2019t wait to see the next thing
      our mayor comes up with.\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nducksonArticle\r\nBox it like
      it\u2019s Hot\r\nAnytime I had extra of something I either ate it or threw
      it somewhere hoping to find it again later. Turns out that\u2019s not very
      efficient, says our mayor. They created a building to store extra inventory
      and now things are easier to find and they won\u2019t get lost. The mayor calls
      it Mr. Duckson\u2019s secret site, not sure how it\u2019s a secret since I\u2019m
      writing about it but I also did not know what storage was either. Please continue
      enlightening us dear mayor!\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nhammerArticle\r\nHammering
      Down\r\nAnother day, another symbol of capitalism. This new statue will help
      us with construction in the future. This mayor has a tougher shell than I thought.
      I guess months in office will do that to you. Maybe this is what our land needs:
      a showmanship of our hard work.\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nstrawCraftArticle\r\nStrawsome\r\nAnd
      for their next trick this mayor with FORCE HIS LABOR UPON US. So long are the
      days of wandering around by choice now we must stay at our stations for hours
      in order to produce more! I thought I was a bad journalist but this is brutal.
      Be prepared to get put to work folks!\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\naltarArticle\r\nAllow
      me to Altar your Mindset\r\nNow this is the kind of stuff this journalist wants
      to see! Ehem not that I know much about this kind of thing of course. In an
      interesting change of events we now have some alters to help boost the amount
      of crumbies we can receive. This might be the most intuitive build yet, I cannot
      praise our mayor enough. I think this is the type of energy that I have been
      waiting to see. I believe that we need to give a little to earn a lot and this
      journalist can see that our mayor feels the same way. I hope to see more of
      this behavior.\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\ndrumArticle\r\nFaster Faster FASTER\r\nQuake
      in adrenaline as you hear the drum roar my fellow Quacklandians. I can feel
      the exhilaration coursing through my veins. I\u2019m writing this article at
      the speed of light dear readers. I\u2019ve never felt so efficient. The drum
      sings to me and it will sing to you too.\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nvillageHallArticle\r\nUp
      is the Only Way We Can Go\r\nThis has been a long time coming. We now have
      a building that shows our greatest achievement: the community that we have
      built together. We have come a long way from the long stretch of grasslands
      to a place we can call home. This hall stands as a momentous occasion for how
      hard we\u2019ve worked and how far we have come. If this message ever reaches
      outside of our humble home I want you to know the beauty of Quacklands and
      we hope we can show it to you.\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\ncrumblingHallArticle\r\nA
      Crumbling Success!\r\nMy fellow ducklings, it is my great pleasure to announce
      the opening of Crumbling Hall. With our growing population we are in need of
      bigger facilities to feed us and our dear mayor has delivered. \u201CI\u2019ve
      been eating so much I can\u2019t even move\u201D says one citizen who sadly
      talked with their mouth full. The line to the Crumbling has been out of the
      door since its construction. \u201CI\u2019ve been standing in line so long
      I don\u2019t even know what day it is!\u201D The duck behind them informed
      me that they had only been there for 20 minutes. Everyone is so excited with
      this new addition. I myself am about to have my fill of the crumbling and I
      will be coming back with a review.\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nFluff\r\nLovely Weather
      Today\r\nThe weather appears lovely today, at least according to the color
      of the grass. The water does not reflect the sky so we are not sure if there
      are clouds, or the sun, or if the sun still remains. It has not been night
      in many years. Most younglings have no concept of such a thing. Either way,
      the grass remains green and the water remains blue, so all much be right in
      the world. \r\nFluff\r\n&\r\nFluff\r\nMany Ducks Still Alive\r\nIt appears,
      given only a cursory glance, that many ducks remain alive. However, no one
      took the time to actually count, so we do not guarantee that many ducks are
      still alive at the time of this publication. \r\nFluff\r\n&\r\nFluff\r\nWater
      A Little Too Cold\r\nComplaints have been rolling in recently about the temperature
      of the water, in lieu of any more pressing matters. It seems that despite the
      eternal consistency of the weather, the water in most of our ponds has cooled
      slightly, and the general population finds this change upsetting. Is it really
      that different? Our editors haven\u2019t been able to tell. The ponds did not
      respond to our request for comment.\r\nFluff\r\n&\r\nFluff\r\nWater A Little
      Too Wet\r\nDissatisfaction has spread among the population regarding the saturation
      of the water. It seems the ponds are completely saturated, with some reaching
      110% saturation, and this fact has caused some speculation and discomfort.
      \u201CI\u2019m not sure what happened,\u201D a passerby said to themself as
      one of our editors listened. Then, becoming contemplative, they continued,
      \u201CMaybe it was always this way. Maybe I just didn\u2019t notice.\u201D\r\nFluff\r\n&\r\nFluff\r\nRocks
      Can\u2019t Be Walked Through\r\nDespite repeated, desperate attempts, rocks
      still cannot be walked through. This we find confusing and upsetting. There
      is nothing in this world that should stop us. We long for freedom. We long
      for power. We long to walk through rocks. \r\nFluff\r\n&\r\nFluff\r\nPeaceful
      Day\r\nHear ye, hear ye, today has been peaceful in Quacklands. By which we
      mean, nothing remotely of value has happened. Nothing. Not one thing. Our editors
      searched high and low for news, and found none. Said editors have now taken
      the day off to swim in one of the identical lakes. \r\nFluff\r\n"
    sourceTxtFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: 897dc624b2a973749942bb9e4496f503, type: 3}
